The upstream ConvNeXt block describes its adaptation from
https://github.com/facebookresearch/ConvNeXt to 1D audio.
This adaptation retains only the Soprano-1.1-80M checkpoint architecture:
kernel-3 ConvNeXt, kernel-1 input projection, and center ISTFT with DC/Nyquist
removal. Unused same-padding ISTFT and alternate decoder configurations were
not copied. All tensor state names and the inference arithmetic are retained.
PyTorch provides the convolutions, normalization, interpolation and ISTFT.

The upstream text utilities attribute their normalization/splitting to
https://github.com/neonbjb/tortoise-tts (tortoise/utils/tokenizer.py and text.py).
The frontend retains upstream cleaning order, sentence lengths and short-unit
merging; regex replaces the stdlib re import to follow repository policy.
Optional text dependencies are loaded when normalization is requested.

Bounded streaming windows are validated against SopranoTTS.infer_stream in
soprano/tts.py at the revision above. The implementation emits sample deltas
and deliberately keeps the native offline predictor-state sequence rather
than adopting the reference HF backend's different consumed-token sequence.
